Z||000004||Standard||09-26-2001||12:57 AM||||We get together because.. well, because it's fun!  What's better than getting together with a bunch of different poeple with similar interests and bs'ing all night?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">         <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||c m west||09-26-2001||01:34 AM||||Everyone from the Fieros West comes over here to WCF EVERY sunday to shoot the pilipheral sh*t - its essentially the club house<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Capt Fiero||09-26-2001||02:43 AM||||We do something similar here in Vancouver BC.  A bunch of us are on ICQ together, as well as we did a Cell Phone Number X-Change, so on any given night we all get ahold of each other and meet up at the local lounge and have a drink, talk turbo's, NOS, V8's suspension mods ya know all the stuff that we all dream about doing, and will do someday.  It is really cool having so many fiero's living so close together, I would almost guess that Vancouver BC Canada has more fiero's per capita than any other place I have ever seen or heard of. <P>------------------<BR>David<BR>85GT<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://photos.onebigvillage.com/pubimage.asp?id_=32415"> <p>[This message has been edited by Capt Fiero (edited 09-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fformula88||09-26-2001||12:31 PM||||Not too many Fiero owners around here to get together... and the few of us that are really haven't gotten together.  I know one of the local guys has gone up to Canada to meet with a few of our cross-border Fiero owners, but I haven't ventured over for that... and now the security at customs will make it take a lot longer to get across the border!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2m6siga.JPG">       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000008||MinnGreenGT||09-26-2001||01:14 PM||||I assume that you could be referring to our "Minnesotan" gathering this Saturday. We try to do this every month or two.  Nice Fieros are rare around here- and gathering a half-dozen or more is great.  Also putting faces to ScreenNames is always cool.  "I actually know what Standard looks like... he's not just a red coupe with a Quad-4!"  <P>Anyway the last time we gathered, we met at Jimmy's house and hung around for a couple of hours, then headed to the local cruising spot (Porkey's in St.Paul on University).  Parked the cars and got out to check out other cars.  Within 10-15minutes, the wind started throwing sand around- and 10 minutes later the rain came.  So most of us went down to Perkins and sat and had coffee/pie/food/etc.  Then finally all headed out a little before Midnight!<P>It's really a lot of fun to just "hang out" sometimes. This could also be the last time we get to gather with Fieros before the long cold winter chills this place to sub-artic temps...  and the snow covers everything in sight!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fullstaff.gif">   <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000009||fierobear||09-26-2001||01:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DXR_DAD:<BR><B>I know quite a few members of the Golden Gate Fieros But most of then I only see once a month??? I do have some fiero buds, that I hang out with every now and then!<BR>But some of you seem to have these little get togethers quite often, and I like that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DXR_DAD</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well hell, Bill, we tried to do a BBQ but it never happened. Care to take the lead? I'd be there. The only problem is deciding which Fiero to bring.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Raydar||09-26-2001||01:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>...before the long cold winter chills this place to sub-artic temps...  and the snow covers everything in sight!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>We just hope that winter won't fall on a weekend this year, in Atlanta.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Not a lot of "hanging out", around me. Lots of people in Atlanta, but not too many Fieros. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000011||NEFA||09-26-2001||01:32 PM||||Our club, NEFA(New England Fiero Association)is starting a monthly dinner. We are going to have the 1st one at the HillTop steakhouse in Saugus MA on Oct. 20th at 4:30PM.<P>We are hoping to get a nice large gathering. If anyone is interested in joining the club or hanging out with other Fiero people come visit. Hope to see lots of friends there.<P>Here is a link of driving directions and it also has a copy of the menu<BR>online <A HREF="http://www.hilltopsteakhouse.com/direction.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.hilltopsteakhouse.com/direction.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/nefa_logo.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/calendar.htm" TARGET=_blank>Upcoming Club Events</A> <P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/tshirt.html" TARGET=_blank>Get your Club T-shirt</A>||||reg||7
Z||000012||skitime||09-26-2001||01:42 PM||||I am lucky enough to live in an area of some very active Fiero maniacs.  We had the first PA BBQ at my house and had over twenty Fieros show up and over 25 people.  We since had a second PA BBQ at the Gilberts and had similar results.  After both BBQs we went to the local cruise night in mass. Next month Oct. 6th for those that are interested, we are having a Tech Session, food , road rally. My house is often the hang out for the Fiero guys with Fieros stopping in all the time. (Slowing secret Fiero mods).  We often also gather at the Gilberts to hang with the Fiero crowd too.  Whenever there are shows, we usually meet for breakfast and gather for a cruise to the show arriving as a group. Nothing prettier than a line of Fieros going down the road. Here are some links to see what it is like.  PS.. We would love more to join our group.<P>Breakfast and Cruise to show <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008057.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008057.html</A> <BR>July BBQ  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008980.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008980.html</A> <BR>August BBQ <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/009803.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/009803.html</A><BR>September Breakfast and Show  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010474.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010474.html</A> <BR>October 6th Tech Session - Mark your calender<P><BR>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-1.JPG">    <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 09-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||DXR_DAD||09-26-2001||02:35 PM||||Well John, Like I said we're just a bunch of "Old Duffers" The youngsters know how to do it!! When was the last time you went on a cruz night??<BR>but any time you want to hang out and maybe help me wash & wax the toy come on over   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Skitime, 20 Fieros at a home BBQ is great!!!!<BR>That's more than alot of the "BIG" shows that I hear about!!!! It just seems that too much is put on the "BIG" out of town shows??<BR>The little weekend get togethers are getting bigger and better from what's been posted here. Maybe we can start doing something like that.<P>Hey John, Give me a call, we'll talk <BR>Check your PM   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DXR_DAD<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 09-26-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000014||skitime||09-26-2001||10:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DXR_DAD:<BR><B>Well John, Like I said we're just a bunch of "Old Duffers" The youngsters know how to do it!! When was the last time you went on a cruz night??<BR>DXR_DAD<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey DXR, Many of us including myself a mid 40s to mid 50s and we love cruise nights. Our group consists of 15 year olds to 55 year olds.  It is amazing how age doesn't matter when we get together.  There is no age barrier it seems when it comes to Fieros. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||DXR_DAD||09-26-2001||10:39 PM||||Skitime, I think you guys have a very good thing going!!! Keep the good times rollin,<BR>Sometimes I wish we had 15 year old members <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>add a little life to things!<P>I really like seeing Fiero owners hanging out like you guys do, I think it's part of owning a fiero. Save a spot for me at the next curz  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DXR_DAD||||reg||14
